Day 1: Introduction to AI for DevOps

Topics

· Why AI is a game-changer for DevOps
---------------------------------------
Traditional DevOps is often reactive — teams fix issues after they occur.

AI can predict failures, detect anomalies early, and trigger remediation before humans even notice.

Example: AI predicts a memory leak before it crashes production and rolls back the release automatically.

Result: Fewer incidents, less downtime, faster MTTR (Mean Time to Recovery).
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Speed Without Sacrificing Stability

DevOps aims for faster releases, but speed often increases risk.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AI Enhances Stability:

Uses historical build/test data to optimize pipelines.

Suggests or enforces best practices (e.g., test coverage, security scanning).

Detects unsafe deployments and blocks them automatically.

Result: Release faster and safer — a dream combo.

